# Corpses of the Lost, ruling 2023-11-10: "You decide to pay 1 life as the last ability is resolving. If you decide to pay 1
# life and Corpses of the Lost is still on the battlefield, it will immediately return to its owner's hand." Turn 1 Bot1
# casts it; turn 3 Faithless Looting discards an Ornithopter (Bot1 descended) and at the end step the trigger is put on the
# stack. Bot2 answers with Petty Theft (Brazen Borrower's Adventure) and returns Corpses of the Lost to Bot1's hand. The
# trigger still resolves (it only needs the descent): Bot1 pays 1 life (19), and the enchantment, no longer on the
# battlefield, is not returned a second time or moved from the hand it is already in: Bot1 holds it once.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Corpses of the Lost
Faithless Looting
Ornithopter
Mountain
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Brazen Borrower
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Corpses of the Lost.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Faithless Looting.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter; Plains)
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Brazen Borrower.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Corpses of the Lost; Ability: Adventure)
Bot1.Accept
[T4 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 19
Bot1.Hand = Corpses of the Lost; Plains; Plains
Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
Exile = Brazen Borrower
